---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — RailKM';
const description =
	'How RailKM handles data: no accounts, no personal data collection, no advertising trackers. Theme preference is stored locally in your browser and route inputs stay in the URL.';
const lastUpdated = '17 October 2026';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} backHref="/" backLabel="Back to Route Mapper">
	<div class="relative mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-4 pt-12 pb-24 sm:px-6 sm:pt-16">
		<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="data-mono text-eyebrow uppercase text-muted">
			<ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
				<li><a class="focus-ring rounded-sm transition-colors hover:text-foreground" href="/">Home</a></li>
				<li aria-hidden="true">/</li>
				<li class="text-foreground">Privacy Policy</li>
			</ol>
		</nav>

		<p class="mt-8 data-mono text-eyebrow font-medium uppercase text-muted">Legal</p>
		<h1 class="mt-5 text-balance text-heading-lg font-semibold text-foreground">Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-muted">
			RailKM is built to work without collecting personal information. This policy explains exactly
			what is — and is not — stored when you use the site.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-3 data-mono text-eyebrow uppercase text-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

		<div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-8">
			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">Summary</h2>
				<ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-2 text-body-md text-muted">
					<li>No account or sign-up is required or offered.</li>
					<li>No personal information is collected, sold or shared.</li>
					<li>No advertising or cross-site tracking cookies are used.</li>
					<li>One small preference is saved locally in your browser.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">Information we collect</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-muted">
					RailKM does not require an account and does not collect names, email addresses, phone
					numbers or payment details. You can use the entire distance engine anonymously.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">Cookies</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-muted">
					RailKM does not set cookies for advertising, analytics or profiling. If a hosting or CDN
					provider sets a strictly necessary operational cookie, it is used only to serve the site
					securely and is not used to identify you.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">Local storage</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-muted">
					RailKM stores a single key in your browser's local storage —
					<code class="data-mono rounded-sm border border-line bg-surface px-1.5 py-0.5 text-body-sm text-foreground">railkm-theme</code>
					— which remembers whether you chose the light or dark interface. It never leaves your
					device and can be cleared at any time through your browser settings.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">Route inputs &amp; URLs</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-muted">
					When you plan a journey, the selected station codes are written to the page URL (for
					example <code class="data-mono rounded-sm border border-line bg-surface px-1.5 py-0.5 text-body-sm text-foreground">?route=NDLS-BPL</code>)
					so the route can be shared or bookmarked. This information is not transmitted to or
					stored on our servers.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">Third-party services</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-muted">
					Fonts are self-hosted and served from this domain. The site may be delivered through a
					content delivery network, which processes standard, non-identifying request logs
					(such as IP address and user agent) for security and reliability.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">Analytics</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-muted">
					RailKM does not run advertising networks or behavioural analytics. Any future
					privacy-respecting measurement would be disclosed here before it is enabled.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">Children's privacy</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-muted">
					The service is not directed at children and collects no personal data from anyone,
					including children.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">Your rights</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-muted">
					Because we do not hold personal data about you, there is nothing for us to export or
					delete. You remain in full control of your browser's local storage and can clear it at
					any time.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">Changes to this policy</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-muted">
					We may update this policy to reflect changes to the service. Material changes will be
					reflected in the "last updated" date above.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="border-t border-line pt-6">
				<h2 class="text-heading-md font-semibold text-foreground">Contact</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-muted">
					Questions about privacy? Reach us at
					<a class="focus-ring rounded-sm text-link transition-colors hover:text-foreground" href="mailto:support@railkm.com">support@railkm.com</a>
					or through the <a class="focus-ring rounded-sm text-link transition-colors hover:text-foreground" href="/contact">contact page</a>.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
